# UI test: `try`, which revision 2 removed with `Result` (SC0155).
#
# The point of this case is the *absence* of a machine-applicable fix. Every
# other migration code in the same block renames a word — `while` becomes
# `loop`, `println` becomes `print`, `function` becomes `def` — and each of
# those carries a `= help:` with a replacement a tool can apply. `try` cannot:
# the new model turns one expression into a binding, a test and a return, and
# which value the function should return on the error path is not something
# the parser can know. So the explanation goes in the note instead, and a
# `= help:` line appearing here would be the regression.
#
# Recovery keeps the operand, so `open(path)` is still parsed and the binding
# still has a value. One diagnostic, not two.

def read_config(path: Str) -> Str:
    let text be try open(path)
    text
